      "documentationUrls": [
        "https://developers.envoy.com/hub/reference/locations-1"
      ],
      "responseContract": "appcall-provider-json-v1",
      "adaptations": [
        "Credential-only healthcheck uses official GET /rest/v1/locations rather than the pinned validator GET /v1/employees?page=1&perPage=1. The current Employees hub page is empty and retrieve-employees documents the deprecated v3 Visitors API at app.envoy.com; locations is the documented cheap authenticated read on api.envoy.com.",
        "Native category is productivity rather than security: Envoy is workplace visitor management, and Rust CATEGORIES has no security bucket."
      ]
    },
    "locations.list": {
      "upstreamActionId": "list_locations",
      "sourceRefs": [
        "action-list-locations",
        "handler-list-locations",
        "request-auth"
      ],
      "documentationUrls": [
        "https://developers.envoy.com/hub/reference/locations-1"
      ],
      "responseContract": "appcall-provider-json-v1",
      "adaptations": [
        "Path is official GET /rest/v1/locations (OpenAPI), not the Client API Key tutorial curl to /v1/locations. Returns raw Envoy JSON under data.",
        "ids array, enabled boolean, and createdAtAfter/createdAtBefore filters are omitted because the native query template cannot express comma-joined arrays without unused inputs and boolean query encoding is not required for the list."
      ]
    },
